  "sections": [
    {
      "title": "Transactions and the Proxy Mental Model",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 0,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Transactions and the Proxy Mental Model",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. The Proxy Model",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Caller",
                    "sub": "hits the proxy",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Proxy",
                    "sub": "begins tx",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Your bean",
                    "sub": "runs method",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Proxy",
                    "sub": "commit or rollback",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Tx is bound to the ==current thread== (`ThreadLocal`) and one `Connection`",
                "New threads and `@Async` calls do {red:NOT} join it"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Defaults and Reach",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Setting",
                "Default"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Propagation",
                  "`REQUIRED`"
                ],
                [
                  "Isolation",
                  "`DEFAULT` (the DB's own level)"
                ],
                [
                  "Rollback",
                  "unchecked only; checked {red:commits}"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Interface proxies: ==public== methods only. Class proxies (Spring 6+): protected and package-private too",
                "`private`, `final`, `static`: ==no transaction==, silently"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Where to Put It",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Annotate the ==service layer==, not controllers or repositories"
              ],
              "style": "check",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "java",
              "lines": [
                "@Service",
                "public class OrderService {",
                "    @Transactional",
                "    public void place(Order o) { ... }",
                "}"
              ],
              "note": "one service method = one unit of work"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "Callers must go through the **proxy**. No proxy, no transaction."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Propagation: REQUIRED, REQUIRES_NEW, NESTED",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Propagation: REQUIRED, REQUIRES_NEW, NESTED",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. The Three Core Modes",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Mode",
                "Outer tx",
                "Inner failure"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "==REQUIRED== (default)",
                  "joined, or new if none",
                  "whole tx **rollback-only**"
                ],
                [
                  "==REQUIRES_NEW==",
                  "suspended, new connection",
                  "independent commit/rollback"
                ],
                [
                  "==NESTED==",
                  "savepoint in outer",
                  "back to savepoint; outer rollback undoes all"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "REQUIRES_NEW is used for {green:audit logs}",
                "NESTED needs **JDBC savepoints**; with JPA, only if the dialect exposes the JDBC connection, as Hibernate's does"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Example: Audit Log",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "java",
              "lines": [
                "@Transactional(propagation = Propagation.REQUIRES_NEW)",
                "public void audit(String event) {",
                "    auditRepo.save(new Audit(event));",
                "}"
              ],
              "note": "audit row commits even if the caller rolls back"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Gotcha and the Others",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "sidebox",
              "title": "REQUIRES_NEW holds two connections",
              "items": [
                "Outer keeps one, inner takes another",
                "Can **exhaust the pool**",
                "Deadlock if outer locks rows inner needs"
              ],
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Mode",
                "Behavior"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "SUPPORTS",
                  "join if present, else none"
                ],
                [
                  "MANDATORY",
                  "throw if none"
                ],
                [
                  "NOT_SUPPORTED",
                  "suspend, run without"
                ],
                [
                  "NEVER",
                  "throw if one exists"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "REQUIRED **joins**, NESTED uses a ==savepoint==, REQUIRES_NEW **splits** into a second transaction."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Isolation Levels",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Isolation Levels",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. The Four Levels",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Level",
                "Dirty",
                "Non-repeatable",
                "Phantom"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`READ_UNCOMMITTED`",
                  "{red:possible}",
                  "{red:possible}",
                  "{red:possible}"
                ],
                [
                  "`READ_COMMITTED`",
                  "{green:blocked}",
                  "{red:possible}",
                  "{red:possible}"
                ],
                [
                  "`REPEATABLE_READ`",
                  "{green:blocked}",
                  "{green:blocked}",
                  "{red:possible}"
                ],
                [
                  "`SERIALIZABLE`",
                  "{green:blocked}",
                  "{green:blocked}",
                  "{green:blocked}"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 3
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Dirty = uncommitted read; non-repeatable = row changed; phantom = new rows. Each level blocks ==one more==",
                "Phantoms at `REPEATABLE_READ`: SQL standard allows; MySQL InnoDB largely prevents",
                "`SERIALIZABLE`: {red:locking or retries}, lowest throughput"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Setting It",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Set per method; `DEFAULT` uses the ==database level==",
                "PostgreSQL: `READ_COMMITTED`. MySQL: `REPEATABLE_READ`"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "java",
              "lines": [
                "@Transactional(isolation = Isolation.READ_COMMITTED)",
                "public void pay(long orderId) { ... }"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Only a NEW transaction",
              "text": "Isolation applies when a ==new== transaction starts. A `REQUIRED` method joining one **ignores** its own setting."
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Interview Point",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Joined method sets SERIALIZABLE?** Ignored; the outer transaction's level wins",
                "**Cost of SERIALIZABLE?** Locking or retries, lowest throughput"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "orange"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Rollback Rules and readOnly",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 3,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Rollback Rules and readOnly",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Default and Overrides",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Case",
                "Result"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`RuntimeException`, `Error`",
                  "{red:rollback}"
                ],
                [
                  "Checked: `IOException`, custom `Exception`",
                  "{green:COMMITS}"
                ],
                [
                  "`rollbackFor = Exception.class`",
                  "checked now rolls back"
                ],
                [
                  "`noRollbackFor = SomeException.class`",
                  "keeps the commit"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Swallowed and Rollback-Only",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`catch` inside the method hides the error from the ==proxy==, so it **commits**",
                "Rethrow the exception to roll back"
              ],
              "style": "cross"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Inner REQUIRED throws",
                    "sub": "marks rollback-only",
                    "ink": "red"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Outer catches",
                    "sub": "carries on",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Outer commit",
                    "sub": "fails",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "UnexpectedRollbackException",
                    "ink": "red"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. readOnly Is a Hint",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`readOnly = true`: Hibernate skips ==dirty checking== and flush",
                "The driver may route the query to a ==replica==",
                "It does **not** block writes on every database"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "Checked exceptions **commit** and a caught exception **commits**. Inner failure in REQUIRED poisons the outer transaction."
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Interview Point: Does an IOException roll back?** No, add `rollbackFor`",
                "**Why UnexpectedRollbackException?** Inner failure already made it rollback-only",
                "**Does readOnly forbid writes?** Not everywhere; it is a hint"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Self-Invocation and Transaction Boundaries",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 4,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Self-Invocation and Transaction Boundaries",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Self-Invocation Bypasses the Proxy",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`this.otherMethod()` skips the proxy, so {red:@Transactional on it is ignored}",
                "Same for ==REQUIRES_NEW== on the inner method: no new transaction"
              ],
              "style": "cross"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Fix",
                "Note"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Move method to another bean",
                  "==preferred=="
                ],
                [
                  "Inject self, or `AopContext.currentProxy()`",
                  "workaround"
                ],
                [
                  "`TransactionTemplate`",
                  "programmatic, explicit"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 0
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Keep Boundaries Tight",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "No remote HTTP or slow I/O inside: ==connection and locks== stay held",
                "{red:LazyInitializationException}: lazy entity touched after the transaction ends"
              ],
              "style": "cross"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Fetch what you need ==inside the service==",
                "Or return **DTOs** instead of entities"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Side Effects After Commit",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "java",
              "lines": [
                "@TransactionalEventListener(",
                "    phase = TransactionPhase.AFTER_COMMIT)",
                "void onOrderPlaced(OrderPlaced e) {",
                "    mailer.send(e);",
                "}"
              ],
              "note": "runs only if the transaction commits"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "Email sent inside the transaction still fires when it later ==rolls back==."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "@Transactional Cheat Sheet",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 5,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "@Transactional Cheat Sheet",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Propagation",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Mode",
                "Does"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "==REQUIRED==",
                  "Joins the existing transaction, or creates one"
                ],
                [
                  "==REQUIRES_NEW==",
                  "Suspends the outer one, starts an independent one"
                ],
                [
                  "==NESTED==",
                  "Savepoint inside the outer transaction"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Isolation Ladder",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "READ_UNCOMMITTED",
                    "sub": "dirty reads",
                    "ink": "red"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "READ_COMMITTED",
                    "sub": "no dirty",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "REPEATABLE_READ",
                    "sub": "no non-repeatable",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "SERIALIZABLE",
                    "sub": "no anomalies",
                    "ink": "green"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Rollback",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "{green:Unchecked} and ==Error== roll back",
                "{red:Checked} exceptions still **commit**",
                "Fix with `rollbackFor`"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "java",
              "lines": [
                "@Transactional(rollbackFor = Exception.class)"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Silent No-Ops",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Self-invocation via `this.method()`",
                "`private` or `final` methods",
                "Objects not managed by Spring",
                "Catching the exception inside the method"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Checklist",
              "text": "==Public service method==, short transaction, `readOnly` for queries, side effects **after commit**."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Check yourself",
      "role": "quiz",
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Check yourself",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "`register()` has no @Transactional and calls `this.audit()`, which is REQUIRES_NEW. Does audit get its own transaction?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "No: `this.` skips the proxy, so the annotation is ignored.",
                "Fix: move `audit()` to another bean."
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "A @Transactional method saves a row, then throws a checked IOException. Is the row saved?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "Yes: checked exceptions commit by default.",
                "Fix: `rollbackFor = Exception.class`."
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "An outer REQUIRED method catches an exception from an inner REQUIRED method and carries on. What happens at commit?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "UnexpectedRollbackException: the shared transaction is already rollback-only.",
                "To recover from the inner failure, use REQUIRES_NEW or NESTED."
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
